From cae069cce65d2bf768fb5c5ab843a05caf01650a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:01:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zune: the original Zune's look, and a top menu of zune, game
 boy and settings

The theme now follows the Zune 30/80/120 - the players with buttons, not
the touchscreen HD: a main menu of large lowercase words over a
background picture, the twist (sub-menus across the top, the list
beneath), shuffle all / play all at the head of every list, the letter
while scrolling fast, and Now Playing with the art over two thirds of the
screen and its options on the center button.

The shelf's top level is three words: zune, game boy, and settings -
last, as on the Zune - which opens TortOS's own menu for the whole
device. Under zune are the collection's words (now playing while
something plays, artists, albums, songs, playlists, genres), each opening
the twist at itself; under game boy the systems, whose games are theirs.
